<title>UK: Standard Chartered jumps after results.</title>
<headline>Standard Chartered jumps after results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Standard Chartered Plc jumped in pre-market dealings after the banking group posted results at the top end of analysts' forecasts.</p>
<p>By 0822  GMT, the shares were up 15p to 785p.  </p>
<p>The banking group said its pre-tax profits rose 32 percent to 870 million stg in the year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Analysts' estimates ranged from 801 million to 870 million.</p>
<p>Dealers said the group's upbeat statement about its prospects in Asia also helped lift the shares. --London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
